From d31572ecfe6ae2d0a5943220b06ebd112a789e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pattems <patrick@crandol.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:07:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/25] [vm,io] Map Linux large file interfaces on FreeBSD

The Linux implementation uses the explicit large file interfaces
(stat64, openat64, pread64, ...). FreeBSD has no *64 variants because
its regular interfaces are always 64-bit. Add platform/largefile.h,
which maps the names on FreeBSD, and include it where they are used.
---
